# core/elements-by-category - What is in this model, grouped the way its notation groups it?
#
# Answers: every element of a model, under the taxonomy category its TYPE belongs to,
# with the category's own label.
#
# Does NOT prove: that an uncategorised element is unimportant. A type no taxonomy
# concept names produces no row here at all, which is why ?uncategorised exists in
# core/inventory's place - use core/elements-by-type or core/inventory when the question
# is "what types are present" rather than "how does this notation group them".
#
# REQUIRES the vocabulary graph role, which converter output does not have: a conversion
# emits instances, not the ontologies and taxonomies they conform to. Attach the published
# vocabulary beside the data - `la-connect` takes several files - and bind
# `graphs.roles.vocabulary`. See examples/with-vocabulary. Without it this template is
# refused rather than returning nothing, and notation/bpmn/process-components is the
# fallback: same question, answered from a hand-maintained list of types.
#
# THIS IS THE TEMPLATE THAT LIST SHOULD NOT HAVE NEEDED. A published taxonomy already
# states which classes each category covers -
#
#   bpmn-tax:Gateways skos:broader bpmn-tax:FlowObjects ;
#       skos:narrower bpmn:ExclusiveGateway, bpmn:ParallelGateway, ... .
#
# - so the grouping is a fact in the vocabulary rather than an opinion in a query. The
# hand-written table it replaces covered 17 of the 49 element classes the BPMN ontology
# declares, omitting every gateway and every sub-process, and invented its own categories
# because it could not see the standard ones. Adding a notation, or a category, is then a
# vocabulary change and needs no template at all - the same claim the classification
# templates make for taxonomies, extended to types.
#
# The category is matched one hop down (`narrower`), not transitively, because a taxonomy
# names classes at the level where the grouping is meaningful; ?parentCategory reports the
# branch above it so a caller can roll up without a second query.
#
# Parameters: MODEL_IRI, LIMIT
{{PREFIXES}}
SELECT ?category ?categoryLabel ?parentCategory ?element ?label ?type
WHERE {
  {{GRAPH_OPEN:vocabulary}}
    ?category {{ROLE:narrower}} ?type .
    OPTIONAL { ?category {{PATH:label}} ?categoryLabel }
    OPTIONAL { ?category {{ROLE:broader}} ?parentCategory }
  {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
  {{GRAPH_OPEN:semantic}}
    VALUES ?model { {{MODEL_IRI}} }
    {{MEMBERSHIP:element}}
    ?element a ?type .
    OPTIONAL { ?element {{PATH:label}} ?label }
  {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
}
ORDER BY ?categoryLabel ?label ?element
LIMIT {{LIMIT}}
